figdown 0.1 block
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: a typed-block opener's LABEL is a positional string, so
# RULE 2.1's mandatory quotes govern it exactly as they govern node, group,
# external, plane, class and bundle. Until now `bitfield b Hdr` and
# `table t Caption` were ACCEPTED with the label "Hdr"/"Caption" — 3 of the
# language's 15 labelled positions — while both genre documents already wrote
# the form as `<keyword> <id> ["label"]`.
# The last line is the failure SYNTAX-STYLE §2.1 says it retired: an unquoted
# multi-word positional is not a spelling, it is a hole. It used to report
# `unexpected argument "Caption"` — a surplus argument, when the defect was a
# missing quote.
bitfield b1 Hdr numbering=msb0
table t1 Caption
timing w1 Lane
table t2 My Caption
